Subject: [sshmap fork 0012] the erased background — BCE paints the WHOLE width (the sparse walk)

Provenance: sshmap (v1.9, ROADMAP task 2) — item (b) of the three pyte cosmetics the dependency audit
            left in the backlog (PYTE82_AUDIT.md, the raise-review of 2026-09-26, "the cheapest and
            the most visible"). Reproduced on the vendored fork first: `erase_in_display` ends its
            loop with `for x in line:` and `line` is a SPARSE `StaticDefaultDict` whose iteration
            yields the KEYS — so only the cells that ALREADY have an entry are written. Measured
            through a bare screen, `ESC[44m ESC[2J` on a blank 30-cell row painted **0 of 30** cells
            (against 6 of 30 for `ESC[K`, which already iterates a `range`), and on a WRITTEN row it
            painted 11 of 30 and left the unwritten cells at the default background: xterm's BCE
            (background colour erase) is what a TUI that clears with a colour — `less -R`, htop, a
            full-screen editor's exit — depends on, and the sparse walk also made the cost of an
            erase depend on the CONTENT of the screen.
            The fix is the one the audit named: an erase writes over the WHOLE width, and the
            attributes it writes are the CURRENT ones (the background survives) minus the character
            and minus the OSC 8 hyperlink of patch 0011 — a cleared cell is a blank, not a link.
            ONE private helper (`Screen._erase_attrs()`) is the single spelling of that cell, used
            by `erase_characters`, `erase_in_line` and `erase_in_display` so the three cannot drift.
            Cost, measured on the dev box (200x50, one `ESC[2J` per feed): **0.016 ms -> 0.229 ms**;
            an 80x24 screen goes **0.010 ms -> 0.061 ms**. Declared: a full-screen clear now writes
            every cell (~10 000 entries at 200x50), which is ~0.5 % of the ~42 ms a full htop chunk
            costs to feed, and the alternative — keeping the sparse walk and painting the DEFAULT
            background only where a cell already exists — is exactly the stale picture this fixes.
            Not taken (the audit's item (c), each its own semantics move): `CSI 3 J` still clears
            the VISIBLE screen as well (xterm clears the saved lines only) and an underline still
            carries into the erased cells (the canvas paints a line across the blank area).
Base:       pyte 0.8.2 (PyPI sdist, sha256 in MANIFEST.md), pyte/screens.py (after patches
            0001-0011; patch 0011 was the last one to touch this file).
Policy:     keep — upstream 0.8.3.dev carries the same sparse loop, so this is a fork fix with no
            release to wait for; the helper is additive and a future rebase can re-apply it alone.
Applied:    2026-10-07, sshmap v1.9.

